================================================================================
# MUSIC PLAYER — HOW IT WORKS
================================================================================

## Architecture

The music system is a multi-source player that can switch between:

1. Local files (mp3 / ogg / wav) — default `_nvL.musicSource = "mp3"`
2. Spotify
3. SoundCloud
4. Apple Music

A central UI (Music Island / Music Player panel) displays cover, title, artist, progress, play/pause, next/prev, queue, and lyrics. The active source drives the UI through a common interface (position, duration, playing state, artwork, queue).

### Local (mp3)
- Files dropped or placed under the executor’s Novoline folder.
- Uses Roblox Sound instances for playback.
- Library + playlists stored locally.
- Source tab inside the player UI.

### Spotify
- Full OAuth 2.0 PKCE flow (no client secret needed in the client).
- Redirect URI hardcoded: `http://127.0.0.1:8888/callback`
- Scopes:
  - user-read-playback-state
  - user-modify-playback-state
  - user-read-currently-playing
  - user-library-read / modify
  - playlist-read-private / collaborative
  - user-read-recently-played
- Tokens + config saved to `Novoline/spotify.json` (refresh token, clientId, user, etc.).
- Uses `HttpService` for all Spotify Web API calls.
- Implements its own SHA-256 + base64url for PKCE.
- Polls currently-playing, controls play/pause/seek/next/prev, manages queue and liked songs.
- Artwork fetched and shown in the UI.
- When Spotify is active source, the player UI mirrors Spotify’s currently-playing + queue.

### SoundCloud
- Search + stream playback.
- Integrated into the same player UI.
- Switching source stops the previous source and announces “Playing from SoundCloud now.”

### Apple Music
- Requires an external helper script (shell + osascript / JavaScript) that the user runs on their machine.
- Helper writes `state.json` and reads `cmd.txt`.
- Client polls state and sends commands (play/pause/seek etc.).
- Notify system tells user to start the helper if not running.
- Same UI surface as the other sources.

### Common UI Matching
- Single Music Island / panel that shows:
  - Cover art (with fade / vinyl sheen effects)
  - Track title + artist
  - Progress bar (TimePosition / duration abstraction)
  - Play / Pause / Next / Prev
  - Queue list
  - Lyrics panel (synced lyrics preferred)
- Source is abstracted: each backend (Spotify, SoundCloud, Apple, local) exposes a common “wrap” that makes the active track look like a Roblox Sound-like object (TimePosition, etc.) so the UI code stays identical regardless of source.
- Immersive tint: when music is playing, the client can tint the whole UI with the dominant color from the cover (`_nv_setTint`).
- Cover only shown when the Music tab is active (`showMusicCover`).

### Persistence
- Spotify tokens → `Novoline/spotify.json`
- Local library / playlists → local files under Novoline/
- Settings (`musicSource`, `musicSpotify`, `musicApple`, etc.) saved in the main config.

